{"name":"Gentle Rain","hex":"#cbc9c5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gentle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tender and amiable; of a considerate or kindly disposition.","Soft and mild rather than hard or severe."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become gentle.","To ennoble."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gentle"},{"term":"rain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Condensed water falling from a cloud.","Any matter moving or falling, usually through air, and especially if liquid or otherwise figuratively identifiable with raindrops."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have rain fall from the sky.","To fall as or like rain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Gentle Rain","blocks":[{"text":"\"The Gentle Rain\" is a 1965 bossa nova composition by Brazilian guitarist Luiz Bonfá, with lyrics by Matt Dubey. Originally written in A minor, this song was first released as part of the motion picture soundtrack of the 1966 film The Gentle Rain by the American director Burt Balaban. The music of this film was a collaboration of Bonfá as composer and Eumir Deodato as orchestra arranger and director."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Gentle_Rain","wikidata":"Q22043873"},{"title":"Gentle Rain (Irene Kral album)","blocks":[{"text":"Gentle Rain is the final album by vocalist Irene Kral performing with pianist Alan Broadbent, which was recorded in 1977 and originally released on the Choice label and re-released by Candid on CD in 2001."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a6/Gentle_Rain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gentle_Rain_(Irene_Kral_album)","wikidata":"Q28448803"},{"title":"Gentle Rain (John Hicks album)","blocks":[{"text":"Gentle Rain is a trio album led by pianist John Hicks, recorded in 1994."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/86/Gentle_Rain_%28John_Hicks_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gentle_Rain_(John_Hicks_album)","wikidata":"Q39073520"},{"title":"Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Rain or rainfall is a form of atmospheric precipitation composed of droplets of water aerosols that have condensed from atmospheric water vapor and fall by gravity. Depending on the intensity, rain can be described as a drizzle, a shower, a cloudburst or a downpour. It is also often accompanied by other weather phenomena such as strong wind (rainstorm) and lightning (thunderstorm), and may be mixed with hail/ice pellet, snow (sleet) and sandstorm. Rain is a major component of the water cycle and is responsible for depositing most of the fresh water on Earth. It provides water for hydroelectric power plants, crop irrigation, and suitable conditions for many types of ecosystems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg/330px-Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain","wikidata":"Q7925"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Konvektionsregen.jpg/500px-Konvektionsregen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Konvektionsregen.jpg/500px-Konvektionsregen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Convective precipitation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKonvektionsregen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Steigungsregen.jpg/500px-Steigungsregen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Steigungsregen.jpg/500px-Steigungsregen.jpg?utm_source=en.wi